  "notes": [
    "Lines are wrapped {recv_ns, msg}; ts_local_recv = recv_ns. Order B lines use the legacy bare listenKey shape (no subscriptionId/event envelope); the importer must accept both.",
    "On CANCELED, Binance puts the cancel request's own client id in c and the order's id in C; client_order_id_chain must not include 'cxl-req-zz91'.",
    "x=REPLACED after PUT /api/v3/order/amend/keepPriority: orderId kept, c changes, q = new total qty. amend_keeps_priority=true (documented). No amend_sent: user stream carries no requests.",
    "STP: x=TRADE_PREVENTION X=EXPIRED_IN_MATCH mapped to expire; prevented qty (A/B) has no column, kept in reason (importer proposal).",
    "Trade id 77000001 occurs on BTCUSDT (order A) and ETHUSDT (order E): Binance trade ids are per symbol, so fill_id uniqueness must be keyed by (venue, instrument, fill_id), not (venue, fill_id).",
    "leaves_qty is not sent by Binance; expected = q - z. ack rows carry qty=q, px=p (importer convention).",
    "orig_qty of order A stays the submit qty (0.5) although it was amended to 0.4; SPEC 3.8 validator rule orig_qty == cum_qty + leaves_qty would warn after the amend (see SPEC gap)."
  ],
